# Notification Unit Testing Rules

## Base Test Structure

### Test Class Setup
```php
namespace MetaFox\{Module}\Tests\Unit\Notifications;

use Tests\TestCase;
use Mockery;
use Illuminate\Contracts\Events\Dispatcher;
use MetaFox\Platform\Contracts\User;
use MetaFox\Platform\Contracts\IsNotifiable;
use MetaFox\Notification\Messages\MailMessage;

class {NotificationType}NotificationTest extends TestCase
{
    protected {NotificationType}Notification $notification;
    protected Dispatcher $eventDispatcher;
    protected User $user;
    
    protected function setUp(): void
    {
        parent::setUp();
        
        $this->eventDispatcher = Mockery::mock(Dispatcher::class);
        $this->app->extend('events', fn () => $this->eventDispatcher);
        
        $this->user = $this->createMockUser();
        // Setup specific mocks for your notification
    }
}
```

### Available Helper Methods
The base `TestCase` class provides several helper methods for notification testing:

1. `createMockNotifiable()`: Creates a mock notifiable instance with standard methods:
   - `preferredLocale()`: Returns 'en'
   - `entityId()`: Returns 1
   - `entityType()`: Returns 'user'

### Required Mock Methods

Model Mock:
```php
$model->shouldReceive('entityId')->andReturn(1);
$model->shouldReceive('entityType')->andReturn('resource_type');
$model->shouldReceive('userId')->andReturn(1);
$model->shouldReceive('userType')->andReturn('user');
$model->shouldReceive('toArray')->andReturn([
    'id' => 1,
    'resource_name' => 'resource_type',
]);
```

## Required Test Cases

### 1. Array Representation
```php
public function testToArray(): void
{
    // Test approved case
    $this->model->shouldReceive('isApproved')->andReturn(true);
    $notifiable = $this->createMockNotifiable(); // Available from base TestCase
    
    $result = $this->notification->toArray($notifiable);
    
    $this->assertEquals([
        'data' => [
            'id' => 1,
            'resource_name' => 'resource_type',
            'message' => 'Expected message',
        ],
        'item_id' => 1,
        'item_type' => 'resource_type',
        'user_id' => 1,
        'user_type' => 'user',
    ], $result);
    
    // Test pending case if applicable
    $this->model->shouldReceive('isApproved')->andReturn(false);
    // Assert pending state
}
```

### 2. URL Generation
```php
public function testToUrl(): void
{
    // Test approved case
    $this->model->shouldReceive('isApproved')->andReturn(true);
    $this->model->shouldReceive('toUrl')->andReturn('https://example.com/resource/1');
    
    $result = $this->notification->toUrl();
    $this->assertEquals('https://example.com/resource/1', $result);
    
    // Test pending case if applicable
    $this->model->shouldReceive('isApproved')->andReturn(false);
    // Test pending URL generation
}
```

### 3. Mail Message
```php
public function testToMail(): void
{
    $notifiable = $this->createMockNotifiable(); // Available from base TestCase
    $this->model->shouldReceive('toUrl')->andReturn('https://example.com/resource/1');
    
    $result = $this->notification->toMail($notifiable);
    
    $this->assertInstanceOf(MailMessage::class, $result);
}
```

### 4. Mobile Message
```php
public function testToMobileMessage(): void
{
    $notifiable = $this->createMockNotifiable(); // Available from base TestCase
    $this->model->shouldReceive('toUrl')->andReturn('https://example.com/resource/1');
    $this->model->shouldReceive('toRouter')->andReturn('@resource/1');
    
    $result = $this->notification->toMobileMessage($notifiable);
    
    $this->assertEquals([
        'message' => strip_tag_content($this->notification->callbackMessage()),
        'url' => 'https://example.com/resource/1',
        'router' => '@resource/1',
    ], $result);
}
```

## Testing Guidelines

### 1. State Testing
- Always test both approved and pending states when applicable
- Test state transitions if the notification handles them
- Verify correct message/URL generation for each state

### 2. Mock Requirements
- Mock only the methods that are actually called
- Use type hints for all mocks
- Set up expectations for method calls that affect behavior

### 3. Assertion Best Practices
- Use specific assertions (assertEquals over assertTrue)
- Test complete array structures
- Verify all notification channels (mail, mobile, web)
- Test localization handling

### 4. Error Cases
- Test with invalid/missing model
- Test with missing permissions
- Test with invalid states
- Test with missing dependencies

